From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 14:14:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] kk: MESA_KK_FRAME_PROBE_S logs draws and scans for
 projections

Red Dead Redemption 2's 3D world is drawn stretched about 3.5 times
horizontally on the phone (PLA-364). Whether its G-buffer viewport or
its camera's projection is wrong decides where to look, and the draw
log (MESA_KK_DEBUG=draws) spends its 400 lines on the launcher long
before the game draws a world.

With MESA_KK_FRAME_PROBE_S=N, every N seconds after the process's first
draw, ten times at most, a probe logs the state of the next 2500 draws
as [kk-draw] lines (render area, attachment, viewport, scissor), and a
thread of its own scans every live host-visible allocation, under the
debug registry's lock, for perspective view-projection matrices: at
each 16-byte offset, row- or column-major, rows 0, 1 and 3 of the xyz
part orthogonal and |row 3| = 1. The most frequent |row 0|, |row 1|
pairs, P00 and P11, are logged as [kk-proj] lines with P11/P00, the
aspect the game projected with. Allocations are registered for this
as for the draw log. 0, the default, does neither.

Class: diagnostics
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-20-rdr2-aspect.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
